--- !u!114 &2438915727490783977
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 3531138164164224124}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 5dea90d657c222e47bb22e7e2a697365, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::InteractionTutorialUI
  videoPlayer: {fileID: 8505078518400919022}
  tutorialVideos:
  - interactType: 2
    videoClip: {fileID: 32900000, guid: 1e98b0c788012a94cb4d89353589c6c3, type: 3}
    tutorialText: With your backpack equipped, press Y / I key to open up your inventory. 
      When picking up smaller and throwable items, they will be added to your inventory. 
      Throwable items can be equipped by pressing A / Left mouse click to select
      them.
  - interactType: 3
    videoClip: {fileID: 32900000, guid: 555364d3c5ea3724fb5af888d50dfff6, type: 3}
    tutorialText: Press the X button / E key to move larger objects around the world.
      Echo can freely place items along with astral projections indicating specific
      locations for larger items to be placed.  Echo can also mantle on top of objects
      pressing the A button / Spacebar.
  - interactType: 4
    videoClip: {fileID: 32900000, guid: ca28d0af9f5943f428b9b84626a6f27b, type: 3}
    tutorialText: Rotate the right Joystick / Press A or D key to move the lockpick
      around the top half of the lock.  Holding Right trigger / Spacebar will confirm
      your selection, the more the inner lock rotates to the left the closer to opening
      the lock.  After finding the correct angle, match the directional inputs to
      jam the lock open.  Be mindful of your lockpicks durability as you will have
      to restart your lockpicking.
  - interactType: 9
    videoClip: {fileID: 32900000, guid: 0cca5345f002a8f41a36cd189f263685, type: 3}
    tutorialText: Hold the Right trigger / Right mouse button to aim your equipped
      throwable object.  Follow the indicator to know where the throwable item will
      land.  Holding the charge longer will result in a more direct throw.
  - interactType: 7
    videoClip: {fileID: 32900000, guid: cbb796da6f23edb4b8ea9bb0a89415c8, type: 3}
    tutorialText: Floating allows you to traverse gaps in the Astral Plane. Press
      the A button / Spacebar next to a gap to begin floating, when the blue line
      is within the green area, press the A button / Spacebar to continue your float.
      You can only float for little while, and failing results in becoming grounded
      again make sure to be careful when crossing large gaps.
  - interactType: 1
    videoClip: {fileID: 32900000, guid: 328164e92fe540b47bcf449b7c870d44, type: 3}
    tutorialText: Press the X button / E key to engage in dialogue with characters
      in the world. When dialogue choices appear, hold the directional input corresponding
      to a choice to select it. Your response time is limited. Pay attention to the
      timer displaying your response time or else a random choice will be selected.
  - interactType: 11
    videoClip: {fileID: 32900000, guid: 34822f877e7d6df48b6b4446883625a5, type: 3}
    tutorialText: Lights of Hope have been left behind and can be found in the shattered
      astral plane, use them to cleanse Echo of their regrets. Match the correct
      inputs to send a burst of energy at the boss and damage it.
  - interactType: 12
    videoClip: {fileID: 32900000, guid: 3accd0f07cfda33439ae7c07fcbcaa76, type: 3}
    tutorialText: Watch out for those void pools, they will do more damage the longer
      that you are in them.
  - interactType: 16
    videoClip: {fileID: 32900000, guid: 42b6a3303108a3d409b2083d4a552657, type: 3}
    tutorialText: Echo can sprint by holding L3 / Left Shift, Echo's sprint meter
      shows how long they can sprint.  Lifting and moving objects drains Echo's stamina
      once depleted Echo will move very slow until their stamina refills.
  - interactType: 10
    videoClip: {fileID: 32900000, guid: 508c83193cace684897d162d76f2d485, type: 3}
    tutorialText: When facing an enemy, they will become highlighted, allowing Echo
      to possess and control their movement.  Hold the Right bumper / Left mouse
      button when they become highlighted. Use the movement inputs to control where
      they will be displaced.  The meter on the left shows how long Echo can possess
      an enemy for.
  - interactType: 6
    videoClip: {fileID: 32900000, guid: 111ad65f646e24044816a40b8cc404a8, type: 3}
    tutorialText: Collectible journal pages can be found throughout the world and
      have different entries based upon your current morality when they are picked
      up.  Press the Select button / Tab key to open your journal and navigate to
      the collectible section to view them.
  tutorial: {fileID: 6673969514948262869}
  descriptionText: {fileID: 4378570431024671786}
  inputDelay: 0.5
